From d217db4dfa0ebc5f69c07fbd05d08e764a70da58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:07:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix egress, approval-resume, sandbox and guardrail gaps

- security/egress: parse IPv6 fully so mapped, translated, NAT64, 6to4,
  Teredo, site-local and multicast forms of private addresses are caught;
  add missing reserved IPv4 ranges; pin connections by re-checking the
  resolved address at connect time (closes the DNS-rebinding window).
- core: RunStateStore.claim() compare-and-set, used by resume() so two
  concurrent resumes cannot both execute an approval; per-process guard
  for stores without claim(). Implemented for in-memory, Postgres, SQLite.
- sandbox: commandTool confines path-like arguments and flag values to
  the workspace (confinePaths, default true).
- security/guardrails: normalise obfuscated text; catch reversed-order,
  rule-injection and non-English override phrasings; detect dotted cards,
  spaced SSNs, and any-case/grouped IBANs verified by mod-97.
- http-tool: fetchImpl option (test transport).
